# DB connection parts (no password — boot.ts resolves it from Secrets Manager
# via DB_SECRET_ID, and services/prisma.ts re-resolves per connection so RDS
# rotation never requires a restart). Shipping these in the bundle makes the
# env change atomic with the application version that requires them.
#
# DB_HOST points at logjam-db-enc — the encryption-at-rest migration target
# (KMS-encrypted, restored from a snapshot of the original logjam-db). The
# logjam_app role + password live in DB content (carried by the snapshot) and
# the app secret logjam/app-db-password is instance-independent, so no
# credential re-wire was needed at cutover. The matching ECS worker task defs
# (infra/terraform/envs/prod/ecs.tf) move via `terraform apply`; apply that
# right after this EB redeploy so API and workers don't straddle two DBs.
# The RDS endpoint is VPC-bound (not publicly routable) and the secret NAME is
# not sensitive; the password itself never appears in config anywhere.
#
# DB_SECRET_ID points at the least-privilege application role secret
# (logjam/app-db-password → logjam_app), NOT the RDS master secret. The EB
# instance role (logjam-eb-role) is granted GetSecretValue on it via
# AppDatabasePasswordAccess (infra/terraform/envs/prod/db_app_role.tf) — that
# grant MUST be applied before this env is deployed or boot.ts fails closed.
# resolveDbCredentials.ts reads BOTH username + password from this secret's JSON.
option_settings:
  aws:elasticbeanstalk:application:environment:
    DB_HOST: logjam-db-enc.chwko8w4iz9p.ap-southeast-2.rds.amazonaws.com
    DB_PORT: "5432"
    DB_NAME: logjam
    DB_SECRET_ID: logjam/app-db-password
